# sumdiff

`sumdiff` is the lightweight comparison, merge and parallel-document editor of the **Sum** ecosystem. It is a separate application built on `sumTUI`; `sumTUI` provides the editor, workspace windows, mouse support, resizing, menus, Markdown rendering and persistent window geometry, while `sumdiff` provides the semantics of related documents.

The design deliberately supports **more than two documents**. This makes it useful not only for version comparison, but also for translations, teaching and comparative programming.


In `0.2.0`, Sum editors can launch the same application directly through the optional sumTUI 0.7 integration. A host can supply the current in-memory text for a real file path, so unsaved edits appear immediately in the comparison while Save still targets the original file. The host can inspect which paths were saved and reload only those documents when `sumdiff` closes.

```bash
sumdiff old.py new.py
sumdiff fr.md es.md en.md
sumdiff BASIC.bas Python.py C.c R.R
```

With two files the default mode is **Compare**. With three or more files the default is **Parallel Documents**. The mode can always be selected explicitly:

```bash
sumdiff --compare old.c new.c
sumdiff --parallel cours-fr.md curso-es.md course-en.md
```

## Compare mode

Compare mode uses a line-oriented diff engine and marks changed lines in a small gutter beside each editor:

```text
~  modified line
+  inserted line
-  removed line
```

Compare mode supports next/previous difference navigation and two-way transfer of the current hunk when exactly two documents are open. Both buffers remain editable and each document is saved independently.

The core diff engine is isolated from the TUI. `DiffResult` exposes hunks, line mapping and intraline spans, so a future renderer can add finer character-level highlighting without changing the application model.

## Parallel Documents mode

Parallel mode is intended for related documents whose text is not expected to be identical, such as translations:

```text
Français.md  <->  Español.md  <->  English.md
```

Scrolling is synchronized between every open document. For ordinary text, `sumdiff` uses relative document position. For Markdown, it uses the document outline first: the current title/section/subsection ordinal and the relative position inside that section are mapped to the corresponding section of the other documents.

That means a French section can remain aligned with the equivalent Spanish and English sections even when the translations use different numbers of lines.

## Markdown

Markdown editors keep the `sumTUI` F2 outline behavior. F2 opens on the title/section that owns the current cursor line.

The active Markdown document also has **Markdown Preview**, including bordered Markdown tables, horizontal/vertical scrolling, and export to HTML/PDF through the `sumTUI` Markdown renderer.

## Windows and layout

Every document is a normal `sumTUI` workspace window. It can be moved with the mouse, resized from the lower-right corner, moved with `Alt+M`, resized with `Alt+Z`, maximized with F11, and selected with F6.

`Window -> Arrange Side by Side` distributes every open document horizontally. `Window -> Arrange Grid` creates a compact grid for larger comparison sets. `Reset Comparison Layout` returns to the side-by-side arrangement.

Window geometry is stored independently under:

```text
$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/sumdiff/workspaces.json
```

or `~/.config/sumdiff/workspaces.json` when `XDG_CONFIG_HOME` is not set.

## Keyboard

```text
F2          Program Map / Document Outline for the active document
F6          Next document window
F7          Next difference
Shift+F7    Previous difference
F8          Apply active hunk to the other document (two-file Compare mode)
F11         Maximize / Restore
Alt+M       Move active window with arrows; Enter accepts, Esc cancels
Alt+Z       Resize active window with arrows; Enter accepts, Esc cancels
Ctrl+S      Save active document
Ctrl+Q      Exit

Alt+F       File menu
Alt+E       Edit menu
Alt+N       Navigate menu
Alt+C       Compare menu
Alt+V       View menu
Alt+I       Window menu
Alt+W       Delete through next word boundary
Ctrl+Alt+W  Delete previous word/separator segment
Alt+H       Help menu
```

The editor keeps the normal `sumTUI` Cut/Copy/Paste and Undo/Redo keys, including `Ctrl+X` for Cut. `Tab` / `Shift+Tab` indents/unindents selected lines. The Edit menu can convert literal tabs to the configured number of spaces, or fixed groups of spaces back to tabs.

## Safety

If one or more documents contain unsaved changes, Exit asks for `SAVE_AND_EXIT`, `FORGET_AND_EXIT`, or `CANCEL` before terminating.

## Architecture

```text
sumTUI
  Workspace / WorkspaceWindow
  TextEditor / ScrollBar
  Program Map / Markdown Outline
  MarkdownView + HTML/PDF export
          |
          v
sumdiff
  ComparisonSession
  DiffResult / DiffHunk
  synchronized line mapping
  Markdown section mapping
  multi-document workspace
  Compare / Parallel Documents
```

`sumdiff` depends on `sumtui`; `sumtui` does not depend on `sumdiff`.

## Development status

`0.2.0` is the current coordinated release. The intentionally small next steps are character-level diff painting, richer hunk controls between panes, opening/closing documents from inside the workspace, and later a three-way merge mode. The underlying data model already keeps the diff engine separate so those additions do not require redesigning the editor.

